WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.337
The President: My fellow Americans, 
a short time ago,

2
00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.640
I ordered the United
States Armed Forces

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:12.145
to launch precision strikes
on targets associated with

4
00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:16.983
the chemical weapons
capabilities of Syrian dictator

5
00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.019
Bashar al-Assad.

6
00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:24.424
A combined operation with
the armed forces of France

7
00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:28.228
and the United Kingdom
is now underway.

8
00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.296
We thank them both.

9
00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.866
Tonight, I want to speak
with you about

10
00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:36.136
why we have taken this action.

11
00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:41.141
One year ago, Assad launched 
a savage chemical weapons attack

12
00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.745
against
his own innocent people.

13
00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:50.717
The United States responded 
with 58 missile strikes

14
00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:55.522
that destroyed 20
percent of the Syrian Air Force.

15
00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:59.325
Last Saturday, the Assad
regime again deployed

16
00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.961
chemical weapons to
slaughter innocent

17
00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:06.533
civilians -- this time, in
the town of Douma,

18
00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:09.869
near the Syrian capital
of Damascus.

19
00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:13.540
This massacre was a
significant escalation

20
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.876
in a pattern of 
chemical weapons use

21
00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.779
by that very terrible regime.

22
00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:24.184
The evil and the
despicable attack

23
00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:27.854
left mothers and fathers,
infants and children,

24
00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:32.559
thrashing in pain
and gasping for air.

25
00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:35.895
These are not the actions
of a man;

26
00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:40.200
they are crimes of 
a monster instead.

27
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:46.105
Following the horrors of
World War I a century ago,

28
00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:50.844
civilized nations joined 
together to ban chemical warfare.

29
00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:54.347
Chemical weapons are
uniquely dangerous

30
00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:57.884
not only because they inflict
gruesome suffering,

31
00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:01.855
but because even small amounts
can unleash

32
00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:05.859
widespread devastation.

33
00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.395
The purpose of our actions
tonight is to establish

34
00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.699
a strong deterrent against
the production, spread,

35
00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:15.535
and use of
chemical weapons.

36
00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:20.139
Establishing this deterrent is 
a vital national security interest

37
00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.175
of the United States.

38
00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:26.446
The combined American, British, 
and French response

39
00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.549
to these
atrocities will integrate

40
00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:34.621
all instruments of
our national power --

41
00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:38.091
military, economic,
and diplomatic.

42
00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:42.028
We are prepared to sustain
this response

43
00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:45.565
until the Syrian regime 
stops its use

44
00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:48.768
of prohibited chemical agents.

45
00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:52.906
I also have a message tonight 
for the two governments

46
00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:57.277
most responsible for supporting, 
equipping, and financing

47
00:02:57.277 --> 00:03:01.080
the criminal Assad regime.

48
00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.317
To Iran, and to Russia, I ask,

49
00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.820
what kind of a nation wants 
to be associated with

50
00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:14.294
the mass murder of innocent men,
women, and children?

51
00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:17.530
The nations of the world
can be judged

52
00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.566
by the friends they keep.

53
00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:23.336
No nation can succeed in
the long run

54
00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:27.273
by promoting rogue states, 
brutal tyrants,

55
00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.209
and murderous dictators.

56
00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:34.280
In 2013, President Putin
and his government promised

57
00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.950
the world that
they would guarantee

58
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.286
the elimination of Syria's
chemical weapons.

59
00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:45.291
Assad's recent attack --
and today's response --

60
00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.561
are the direct result of
Russia's failure

61
00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.164
to keep that promise.

62
00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:54.801
Russia must decide if it
will continue down

63
00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:58.972
this dark path, or if it will
join with civilized nations

64
00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:02.942
as a force for
stability and peace.

65
00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:06.479
Hopefully, someday we'll
get along with Russia,

66
00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:11.050
and maybe even Iran
-- but maybe not.

67
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:16.122
I will say this, the United States 
has a lot to offer,

68
00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:19.559
with the greatest
and most powerful economy

69
00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:22.428
in the history
of the world.

70
00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:27.000
In Syria, the United
States -- with but a small

71
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.938
force being used to eliminate 
what is left of ISIS --

72
00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:35.074
is doing what is
necessary to protect

73
00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.676
the American people.

74
00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:40.413
Over the last year,
nearly 100 percent

75
00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:46.185
of the territory once controlled
by the so-called ISIS caliphate

76
00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:49.522
in Syria and
Iraq has been liberated

77
00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.924
and eliminated.

78
00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:55.294
The United States has also
rebuilt our friendships

79
00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.397
across the Middle East.

80
00:04:57.397 --> 00:05:00.633
We have asked our partners to 
take greater responsibility

81
00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.336
for securing their home region,

82
00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:07.607
including contributing large 
amounts of money

83
00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:09.809
for the resources, equipment,

84
00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:14.614
and all of the
anti-ISIS effort.

85
00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:17.417
Increased engagement from
our friends,

86
00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:21.921
including Saudi Arabia, 
the United Arab Emirates, Qatar,

87
00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:25.525
Egypt, and others can
ensure that Iran

88
00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:29.929
does not profit from the
eradication of ISIS.

89
00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:35.201
America does not seek an
indefinite presence

90
00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:38.705
in Syria under no
circumstances.

91
00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:42.275
As other nations step up
their contributions,

92
00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:45.778
we look forward to the day
when we can bring

93
00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.880
our warriors home.

94
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.217
And great
warriors they are.

95
00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:54.887
Looking around our very
troubled world,

96
00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.223
Americans have no illusions.

97
00:05:57.223 --> 00:06:01.527
We cannot purge the world
of evil or act everywhere

98
00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:04.263
there is tyranny.

99
00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:07.133
No amount of American
blood or treasure can produce

100
00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:11.270
lasting peace and
security in the Middle East.

101
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.372
It's a troubled place.

102
00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:17.777
We will try to make it better, 
but it is a troubled place.

103
00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:21.447
The United States will be
a partner and a friend,

104
00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:25.284
but the fate of the region
lies in the hands

105
00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.353
of its own people.

106
00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.956
In the last century, we
looked straight into

107
00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:34.093
the darkest places of
the human soul.

108
00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:37.797
We saw the anguish that
can be unleashed

109
00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:41.267
and the evil that can take hold.

110
00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:47.740
By the end of the World War I, 
more than one million people

111
00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:52.345
had been killed or injured 
by chemical weapons.

112
00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:57.984
We never want to see that
ghastly specter return.

113
00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:01.554
So, today, the nations of
Britain, France,

114
00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:04.657
and the United States of America
have marshaled

115
00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:10.129
their righteous power against
barbarism and brutality.

116
00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:12.698
Tonight, I ask all
Americans to say a prayer

117
00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:17.103
for our noble warriors and
our allies as they carry out

118
00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.504
their missions.

119
00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.841
We pray that God will
bring comfort to those suffering

120
00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.142
in Syria.

121
00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:26.245
We pray that God will
guide the whole region

122
00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:29.849
toward a future of
dignity and of peace.

123
00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:33.352
And we pray that God will
continue to watch over

124
00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:37.557
and bless the United
States of America.

125
00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:39.659
Thank you, and goodnight.

126
00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:40.793
Thank you.
